    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1147">

                <pb facs="1166" n="1156" sameAs="frus:frus1949v09/pg1156"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">841.8591/10–2949: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at Shanghai</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">McConaughy</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the
                        Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Shanghai</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1949-10-29T17:00:00+08:00">October 29, 1949—5
                            p. m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received October 29—8:21 a. m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>4598. Mytel 4583, October 28.<anchor n="91" xml:id="d1147-f1"/> Two British
                    steamers arrived Shanghai October 29 from Hong Kong: (1) small tanker <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Louise Moller</hi>, cargo 2095 tons Diesel oil in bulk
                    for Texas Company, expected to sail October 30 at 0300 hours; (2) SS <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Tsinan</hi> with general cargo. Pilot who brought in <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Moller</hi> informed Consulate General <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Moller</hi> entered Yangtze attended by British warship.
                    Chinese warship on patrol ordered <hi rendition="#italic">Moller</hi> to stop or
                    would open fire. British warship <pb facs="1167" n="1157" xml:id="pg1157"/> then
                    ran between two vessels and trained guns on Chinese warship. Meanwhile SS <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Tsinan</hi> had come in from sea and joined procession.
                    British warship escorted both vessels some distance into estuary before leaving
                    them. Entry merchant vessels thus made under threat of force by British naval
                    vessel. Further details subsequent telegram. American SS <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Flying Cloud</hi> due mouth Yangtze morning October 30.</p>
                <p>Sent Department 4598; repeated Hong Kong 349; Department pass Chungking 44.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">McConaughy</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d1147-f1" n="91" xml:id="d1147-f1-content">
                <p>Not printed; it reported the <hi rendition="#italic">Flying Cloud</hi> had been
                    delayed by adverse weather in its voyage from Hong Kong (393.115/10–2449).</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
